WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.897 --> 00:00:02.110
- [Mark] All right, JJ.

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.864
JJ, what neighborhood did you grow up?

00:00:03.864 --> 00:00:04.697
What neighborhood?

00:00:04.697 --> 00:00:09.470
- Oh, just I say Westside LA, yeah.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.123
- [Mark] And gang life
started for you at what age?

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.699
- [JJ] I would say,
introduced in kindergarten.

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:19.042
(Mark and JJ laugh)

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:19.875
- [Mark] Really?

00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:23.110
- Yeah , I used to see
stuff on TV, you know.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:23.943
And uh,

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.310
you see movies

00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:32.560
and you emulate the styles, the glamor,

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.957
the attention.
- Right.

00:00:35.718 --> 00:00:37.568
- Then it's time to protect yourself.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.470
You gotta know how to protect yourself.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.010
Lookin' at people come from,

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.740
older people, older influences.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.473
I call 'em negative
influences and bad influences.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.133
You start, uh,

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.757
learning from 'em.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:06.134
What to do, what not to do,
how to protect yourself.

00:01:06.134 --> 00:01:07.410
- [Mark] Tell me about your family.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.290
Did you have both parents?

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.183
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:12.406 --> 00:01:14.720
- [Mark] And you still
got involved in gangs?

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.800
Your parents didn't
steer you clear of that?

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.005
- Nah, they just been around.

00:01:19.005 --> 00:01:20.031
- [Mark] Just the way it is.

00:01:20.031 --> 00:01:21.863
- You look out the door
that's all you see.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.523
It was like say '79, not '78, but '79,

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:29.890
it was goin' on.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.540
- [Mark] I mean, do you,
when you were a kid,

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:32.660
do you have role models?

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.430
Do you have neighbors or friends
that the dads were lawyers

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.014
or doctors or, none of that.

00:01:38.014 --> 00:01:38.847
- None of that.

00:01:38.847 --> 00:01:39.680
- [Mark] None of that.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:40.513
- None of that.

00:01:40.513 --> 00:01:41.440
There were no daddies around.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.840
They was probably all dead or in jail.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.643
You know, that's the plan.

00:01:45.643 --> 00:01:46.810
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:49.339
Have you done prison time?

00:01:49.339 --> 00:01:51.113
- Yeah, I did some prison time.

00:01:51.113 --> 00:01:52.080
Two times.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.760
I had a probation violation.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.680
And I was hangin' out, not reporting.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.033
Did 16 months, they sent me to prison.

00:02:04.648 --> 00:02:06.723
It was all right, it's back in the days.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.810
Let's see, I stayed out
five years, I went back.

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:13.543
Did like ten.

00:02:13.543 --> 00:02:15.563
I gotta an assault and battery,

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.533
and did that.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.930
Ten, came on back.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:22.763
- [Mark] Ten years?

00:02:22.763 --> 00:02:23.596
- Yeah.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.750
I never went back.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.350
I've been out for like 12 years.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.900
Ain't nothin' in there,
you know what's I'm sayin'?

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:33.760
(Mark laughs)

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.080
- Why be around a whole
bunch of home boys?

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.303
I like honeys.

00:02:40.015 --> 00:02:40.980
- [Mark] Not a lot of those in prison.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.330
- Yeah, I'm like, I'm cool.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:44.840
I got along with a lot of people.

00:02:46.891 --> 00:02:47.724
All races.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.820
Vietnamese, Mexican,

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.160
white.
- Really?

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:53.993
- Yeah, black.

00:02:53.993 --> 00:02:55.120
I got along with everybody.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.300
I call it like being multi culture.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.683
I don't play the color
line or the race thing.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.113
I just like people.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:12.120
And you gotta like yourself first.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.193
You gotta care.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:20.040
I was with moms, pops, and
they had they're ups and downs.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.340
They wasn't perfect, they was young.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.703
So you get involved with.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.280
You better not be one and
part of the gangs, though.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.113
So it was like under the radar.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:35.363
Oh.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.340
I used to smoke weed.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:43.210
And it took me down.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:44.053
It's like, ah,

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.830
I stopped having a drive
to go get the money,

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.203
to hustle, to go get the job.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:54.340
I tried to draw.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.343
I tried to use at as an excuse to, nah.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.883
It took my creativity away.

00:03:59.883 --> 00:04:00.890
- [Mark] That's what I see.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:02.248
- And it's an addiction.

00:04:02.248 --> 00:04:03.490
- [Mark] That's the thing
people don't realize.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:04.837
- It took my-

00:04:04.837 --> 00:04:06.090
- [Mark] It takes drive away.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:06.923
- Yeah.

00:04:06.923 --> 00:04:07.756
Sleep.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.660
- [Mark] Your drive to create.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:14.220
- Yeah, I stopped using that.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.900
But I still had a temper.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.370
I still was mad.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.240
And I used to get angry.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:20.173
So it lead me,

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:23.367
to take that case.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:26.523
While I was there,

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:29.723
I found myself.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.293
I looked at myself.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:37.240
You get in that tight spot, a jail cell

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:39.560
or a casket (laughs).

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.610
You look at yourself,
you're in a tight spot.

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:45.470
So I start understanding myself.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:46.370
I started

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.473
knowing myself and accepting myself.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:56.410
And I guess, I started
caring more about myself.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:59.430
And lookin', I'm not
gonna let this happen.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.740
And I used to just walk and look

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:03.870
and see those cars go by, trucks.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:07.000
So I'm gettin' me one of
those, maybe a couple.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.490
I ain't comin' back.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.623
So, I got out.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:11.823
I cut grass.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.433
I did a whole bunch of work.

00:05:16.571 --> 00:05:19.390
Applications, applications.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:22.204
It's like, "We do it on the computer,

00:05:22.204 --> 00:05:24.480
'cause you gotta do it on a computer."

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.960
I say, "Can I get an application,
I wanna fill it out."

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.140
They don't so that
anymore, they laugh at me.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.067
Some people (swooshes),

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:32.430
"We're not hiring," and
they just slam the door.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.230
So it start getting funny to me.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.210
I kinda got it.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.730
No, I'm not gonna get discouraged.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.467
I'm gonna see if they
slam this door on me.

00:05:40.467 --> 00:05:42.460
"Slam it," (laughing) I said.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.230
I'm gonna see if they're gonna (shoos).

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.840
I couldn't get no work.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.283
So I said, I got one
though, a temporary job.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.427
I looked at the check that week, I say,

00:05:54.427 --> 00:05:56.713
"I make this every day," me and my father.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.410
I got me a truck.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:03.243
He had a truck.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.110
He had a lot of tools.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:08.960
He said, "I fucked up all the money."

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.780
He said, "I messed up all the money,

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.887
"so this is all I got is these tools.

00:06:15.887 --> 00:06:19.140
"If I go, everythin' is all yours."

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.780
So we worked.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.350
We moved, we painted.

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:26.370
We oversee all kind of like
apartment complex buildings

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:27.220
and stuff.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.060
Did everything, plumbing.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:32.100
And he had so many tools, we
just got work, work, work.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:35.090
And that kept me out.
- Yeah.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:35.923
- Roof in.

00:06:37.414 --> 00:06:40.650
Then I learnt, I learnt this all out here.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:42.406
I couldn't focus in there.

00:06:42.406 --> 00:06:44.290
There was too much stuff goin' on.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.123
- [Mark] In prison?

00:06:45.123 --> 00:06:48.243
- Yeah, riots and fights, and
you know, it was just crazy.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.700
You got people wanna be rappers

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:52.780
and you tryin' to read the book,

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:56.360
and he's over here makin'
noise beatin' on a desk.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.600
So I couldn't concentrate.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.560
And then you gotta watch
your back all the time.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.530
And I still carry myself like that.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.270
I won't drink, I won't smoke.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:06.970
I won't smoke a joint, I
won't smoke a cigarette.

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.670
It's like I'm still in the yard.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:09.503
I pay attention.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.570
Yeah, you gotta be aware
of your surroundings.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.660
It's like you're in a war zone.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:20.660
And I seen a lot of like,
gore, you know, I seen it.

00:07:20.734 --> 00:07:21.583
- [Mark] In prison, mostly?

00:07:21.583 --> 00:07:23.623
- Streets, prison, I seen it.

00:07:25.308 --> 00:07:26.141
And it ain't that nice.

00:07:26.141 --> 00:07:26.974
When I see

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.720
the environment that I'm around,

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.700
like right here right now,

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:35.630
if I see somethin' startin' to look funny,

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:36.900
I gotta go.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:40.430
I'm not gonna stand
around and get blown up.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.690
Because you got a lot of idiots out here

00:07:43.665 --> 00:07:45.370
and I don't wanna be around 'em.

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:49.060
I'm gone (swooshes), you
know what I'm sayin'?

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:51.505
And I got a little gray haired now.

00:07:51.505 --> 00:07:52.338
- [Mark] How old are you?

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:53.723
- 47.
- 47.

00:07:53.723 --> 00:07:54.870
- Yeah, I'm a little gray haired now

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.760
and it's wisdom, I call it.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.510
I don't do the things I used to do.

00:08:01.856 --> 00:08:03.650
I don't have nothin' to prove.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:05.240
- [Mark] Yeah, I think we're
all young and stupid once.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.823
- Yeah, I was very.

00:08:07.665 --> 00:08:09.880
I was, I guess, searching for the

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.640
attention-deficit
disorder that we all had.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.870
We're searching for attention

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.630
and you're gonna get that attention

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:18.590
but it's a lot a consequences

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:20.800
gonna come with that attention.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.740
And then you start taking them steps

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:25.300
and then I gotta do all these things.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:28.570
Because if you don't,
you gonna get beat down.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:29.573
Anything can happen.

00:08:33.469 --> 00:08:35.020
It's survival.

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:37.550
There's a lot of people
got talent around here.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.140
I look at everybody like, around here,

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:41.450
I look at 'em like they're my family.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.530
Even if I don't know 'em, I
still look at 'em as my family,

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:48.070
because we're the ones from the family

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:50.450
that the family really like shunned us.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.780
We're the black sheep of the family.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.650
We speak the same language.

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:54.680
We all got somethin' in common.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.200
We speak the same language

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.610
in this flock of the sheeps right here.

00:08:57.610 --> 00:08:58.880
We're the black sheeps.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:01.800
Everybody else, they got
their houses, their kids.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:05.433
They got their jobs and they're
eatin' all this nasty food.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.150
They're all messed up.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:12.700
Reason why I'm so strong is
because I had it so hard.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:13.853
I had it real hard.

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.552
I'm talkin' about real hard.

00:09:17.552 --> 00:09:19.490
And I asked nobody for nothin'.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.490
I don't ask somebody

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:23.010
not for one penny,

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:24.760
a quarter or a dollar.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.530
I never, my father always taught me

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:27.804
never to ask nobody for nothin'.

00:09:27.804 --> 00:09:29.410
Go out there and get it yourself.

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:30.300
Even when it came to him.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.317
He'll give me, but he'll say,

00:09:32.317 --> 00:09:34.462
"I gotta stop givin',
you grown, git your own.

00:09:34.462 --> 00:09:36.927
"Go git your own, I gotta stop.

00:09:36.927 --> 00:09:40.320
"I could loan you somethin',
you better give it back."

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:42.098
'Cause I loaned him and he said,

00:09:42.098 --> 00:09:43.957
"Like I give it back to
you, you give me mines back,

00:09:43.957 --> 00:09:46.260
"you need anything." (claps)

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:49.260
But when we loaned money to each other,

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:50.450
we always give it right back.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.320
We never try to play
games with each other.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.865
- [Mark] So you saw values

00:09:55.865 --> 00:09:56.910
and you're walking a straight line.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:10:01.140
How much do you credit
your dad being in your life

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:02.470
with all that?

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:04.946
You had a good role model, it sounds like.

00:10:04.946 --> 00:10:05.830
- You know, but I kinda didn't listen

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.690
because I did things
behind his back still.

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:10.947
But I always come up
out of and then he asks,

00:10:10.947 --> 00:10:12.950
"Why you gettin' in trouble so much?"

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:15.427
Or, "Why you doin' this,
why you actin' like that?"

00:10:15.427 --> 00:10:17.550
"Why you dressin' like that?"

00:10:19.175 --> 00:10:20.210
It's like, "You hang with these dudes,

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:21.730
you don't hang with those."

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.550
I said, "I'm not hangin'
with none of them,

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:25.316
'I'm hangin' by myself,

00:10:25.316 --> 00:10:28.047
"but gimme some money,
I'm behind right now."

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:31.333
- [Mark] But you sound like

00:10:31.333 --> 00:10:32.166
you got your head in the right place

00:10:32.166 --> 00:10:33.310
and you've been this way for awhile.

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.896
What would you credit,

00:10:35.896 --> 00:10:37.896
where would you think you got that from?

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.443
- I would say,

00:10:42.097 --> 00:10:43.940
I'm just tired.

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:45.850
Being around a lot of people,

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:46.683
a lot

00:10:47.873 --> 00:10:49.260
of people who lost a lot.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:51.760
People that got cheated a lot.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:53.910
People who just had a chance

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:57.720
but they were so messed up on drugs.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:01.500
They always told me, "Don't
do this, don't do that."

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:05.410
Don't snort this, don't
shoot this, don't drink this.

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:08.010
And those people, they're all dead now.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:08.843
They got killed.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:12.850
Got a whole bunch of time
in prison for nothin'.

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:16.403
Two strikes when the law's in effect.

00:11:18.219 --> 00:11:19.052
And they ain't never comin' home

00:11:19.052 --> 00:11:20.785
and they're like legends.

00:11:20.785 --> 00:11:22.300
They taught me.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:24.140
They showed me how to work on cars.

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:25.280
Lowriders and stuff.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:26.640
I was a little kid

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.130
and he give me a box
of lowriders from 1977.

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:31.463
He gave me three boxes.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.640
Big boxes, bigger than these,

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.543
just full of all lowriders.

00:11:37.407 --> 00:11:39.670
And my mother told me,
"Don't bring 'em home."

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:43.600
I said but, "But they'll be
worth somethin' in the future."

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:45.713
Don't bring no more junk here.

00:11:46.867 --> 00:11:48.350
And that still hurted me to this day,

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.600
